{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion","id":1028624,"title":"Medicine skill confusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T11:43:06-08:00","id":1028624,"title":"Medicine skill confusion","content":"I do not understand how many successes are needed with the Medicine skill to stabilize someone who is bleeding out. Probably because the rules (or at least the stated rule &amp; proffered example) contradict themselves:<br /> <br /> World of Darkness Storytelling System Rulebook, p.62, 2nd column, 1st complete paragraph in that column, 3rd sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;... a patient who's bleeding to death or in a coma is stabilized if one success is achieved on the roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Same page, same column, 5th paragraph (which starts an Example section), 5th sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;He must accumulate seven successes to stop the flow of blood and save Emir's life.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, um - WTH? Do you stabilize someone with 1 success, or do you have to get successes = their total health dots? This would make a HUGE difference in a life-or-death situation (seriously, poor Emir almost bleed out &amp; died waiting for those 7 successes).<br /> <br /> Is there an erratum for this somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T12:26:57-08:00","id":1028649,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you're referencing 1st Edition. You should probably specify so explicitly, because people will tend to assume the most recent iteration of the rules otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T12:33:14-08:00","id":1028653,"title":"","content":"In that case I'd probably suggest to go by the rule presented and not the flawed example. Also, non extended actions only require one success in general. Since someone bleeding out seems a bit more pressing than extended actions seems to cover I'd say that reinforces that that the example is flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T13:48:35-08:00","id":1028676,"title":"","content":"OK, I managed to get a look at a friend's 2nd edition (sorry, didn't realize I had the wrong one until now - oops).<br /> <br /> And... now I'm just as confused. Scratch that: even more so than before. Far, far more so.<br /> <br /> There is literally NO mention of what using the Medicine skill does to save someone bleeding out.<br /> <br /> In the Medicine skill section, it mentions that someone with one dot can use their skill to stop someone from bleeding out. No details on how.<br /> <br /> OK, let's check the Injury and Healing section:<br /> <br /> It talks about using Medicine to heal, it mentions using Medicine + Dexterity for ER or first aid, but nothing that says 'here's what happens when you treat someone in the field who is unconscious &amp; bleeding out'.<br /> <br /> So, does that mean treat that situation like healing any other injury &amp; just try to downgrade their rightmost box to bashing? Because, rather importantly, if you're not in a hospital you can't treat a lethal wound.<br /> <br /> Which... yeah, that last makes first aid a bit problematic, doesn't it? You literally CANNOT stop someone from bleeding to death once their health boxes are all full &amp; the rightmost box is an X, because you can't even treat a lethal wound in the field.<br /> <br /> In fact... since treating wounds in a hospital is an extended action with rolls occurring once per hour, and bleeding out occurs in a time frame of minutes... yeah, when your last box has an X in it, you're already dead &amp; just don't know it yet by RAW.<br /> <br /> CoD 2e book, p.95, 2nd column, 2nd full paragraph, 3rd sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;When a character's rightmost Health box has lethal damage marked in it, he takes another point of damage each minute... until he receives medical attention, mundane or supernatural.&quot;<br /> <br /> OK, so this implies medical attention can treat bleeding out. How?<br /> <br /> Same page, 6th paragraph:<br /> <br /> &quot;The only exception is if a character has all her Health boxes full of lethal damage - she's bleeding out. She can't recover from that without urgent medical attention and emergency surgery.&quot;<br /> <br /> Got it, medical care needed. Still don't know how that works.<br /> <br /> Finally, p.96, 1st column, the entire section on Medical Care (which, obviously, I'm not quoting that much):<br /> <br /> ZERO word on treating someone bleeding out. Zip. Zilch. Nada.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do I tag this for the Errata Gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T14:59:41-08:00","id":1028702,"title":"","content":"Just two monthes ago I asked similar questions - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1008815-2e-battlefield-medicine-from-lethal-to-bashing\">here is topic about Medicine usage on Battlefield</a>, maybe it helps you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T15:47:41-08:00","id":1028719,"title":"","content":"Ah, found something that will work.<br /> <br /> Armory Reloaded, p.151 - &quot;Bleeding Out&quot;. It's meant as a 'hack', but I think the medical treatment portion of it could easily work for any time a character is incapacitated &amp; unconscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T17:48:34-08:00","id":1028802,"title":"","content":"I was, literally, just reading this over last night. I had some similar questions, but I think(?) I talked it all out in my head.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that if you're full of lethal, you're bleeding out. Once you're bleeding out, damage doesn't automatically downgrade, and in fact your lethal upgrades to aggravated at the rate of one per minute, until you get medical attention or you fill up...then you die.<br /> <br /> &quot;When a character's rightmost Health box has lethal damage in it, he takes another point of damage to each minute (upgrading existing lethal damage to aggravated) until he receives medical attention...&quot; (&quot;Full Health Tracks...,&quot; CofD, of. 95).<br /> <br /> &quot;Normally, a character can heal without medical attention, though the use of the Medicine Skill helps her recover... The only exception is if a character has all her Health boxes full of lethal damage \u2013 she's bleeding out. She can't recover from that with an urgent medical attention and emergency surgery.&quot; (&quot;Healing,&quot; CofD, pg. 95)<br /> <br /> On page 96, it details what can be done to heal a character from this prediciment:<br /> <br /> &quot;Medical care is an extended action requiring success is equal to the total number of damage suffered by the patient. In the field or ER, the dice pool Dexterity + Medicine, and the interval is one minute. <br /> &quot;Achieving sufficient successes restores one Health point lost to bashing damage...&quot; (&quot;Medical Care,&quot; CofD, pg. 96).<br /> <br /> I get, from this, the following scenario:<br /> Jack has been shot and left in the alley to die. He's taken 8 lethal damage - all his Health Pool - and is unconscious from failing his Stamina roll. Two minutes go by and two points of lethal get upgraded to aggravated damage. <br /> Fortunately for Jack, an off-duty nurse walks by peers down the alley, and sees Jack bleeding out on the ground. By the time she cautiously approaches, and realizes what's going on, Jack's lost another two points of lethal to aggravated damage. But the nurse starts doing what she can. <br /> The first minute of aid she gets four successes - not enough to pull Jack out of danger, as she needs successes equal to Jack's damage (and he loses another point to aggravated, and now has 5 aggravated damage and is slipping away). The next round the nurse - determined not to let Jack die - uses a point of Willpower and pulls in 5 successes! The rightmost box, still with lethal damage, gets upgraded to bashing damage. Jack will stop losing losing Health Points and is out of danger...for the moment.<br /> <br /> Maybe my interpretation is wrong, but this is how I came to understand it! Hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12124,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","user":"Lord Dynel","date":".  All kinds of errors! 01-08-2017, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T19:55:09-08:00","id":1028845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Dynel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion?p=1028802#post1028802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was, literally, just reading this over last night. I had some similar questions, but I think(?) I talked it all out in my head.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that if you're full of lethal, you're bleeding out. Once you're bleeding out, damage doesn't automatically downgrade, and in fact your lethal upgrades to aggravated at the rate of one per minute, until you get medical attention or you fill up...then you die.<br /> <br /> &quot;When a character's rightmost Health box has lethal damage in it, he takes another point of damage to each minute (upgrading existing lethal damage to aggravated) until he receives medical attention...&quot; (&quot;Full Health Tracks...,&quot; CofD, of. 95).<br /> <br /> &quot;Normally, a character can heal without medical attention, though the use of the Medicine Skill helps her recover... The only exception is if a character has all her Health boxes full of lethal damage \u2013 she's bleeding out. She can't recover from that with an urgent medical attention and emergency surgery.&quot; (&quot;Healing,&quot; CofD, pg. 95)<br /> <br /> On page 96, it details what can be done to heal a character from this prediciment:<br /> <br /> &quot;Medical care is an extended action requiring success is equal to the total number of damage suffered by the patient. In the field or ER, the dice pool Dexterity + Medicine, and the interval is one minute.<br /> &quot;Achieving sufficient successes restores one Health point lost to bashing damage...&quot; (&quot;Medical Care,&quot; CofD, pg. 96).<br /> <br /> I get, from this, the following scenario:<br /> Jack has been shot and left in the alley to die. He's taken 8 lethal damage - all his Health Pool - and is unconscious from failing his Stamina roll. Two minutes go by and two points of lethal get upgraded to aggravated damage.<br /> Fortunately for Jack, an off-duty nurse walks by peers down the alley, and sees Jack bleeding out on the ground. By the time she cautiously approaches, and realizes what's going on, Jack's lost another two points of lethal to aggravated damage. But the nurse starts doing what she can.<br /> The first minute of aid she gets four successes - not enough to pull Jack out of danger, as she needs successes equal to Jack's damage (and he loses another point to aggravated, and now has 5 aggravated damage and is slipping away). The next round the nurse - determined not to let Jack die - uses a point of Willpower and pulls in 5 successes! The rightmost box, still with lethal damage, gets upgraded to bashing damage. Jack will stop losing losing Health Points and is out of danger...for the moment.<br /> <br /> Maybe my interpretation is wrong, but this is how I came to understand it! Hope this helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I thought at first, but there are a few problems...<br /> <br /> Firstly, the line you mention, 'Achieving sufficient successes restores one Health point lost to bashing damage.&quot; Bleeding out isn't bashing damage, it's all lethal - therefore this does not apply.<br /> <br /> Secondly, lethal damage can only be treated in a hospital or similar facility (p. 96, &quot;Thus, a lethal wound can be downgraded to bashing, and an aggravated wound can be downgraded to lethal. Such treatment can occur only in a hospital...&quot;). So the nurse could not treat Jack for his lethal wounds in the alley.<br /> <br /> Finally, p.96 again, &quot;An extended Intelligence + Medicine roll is made. The number of successes required is five for a lethal wound... Each roll takes an hour.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ergo, bleeding out:<br /> - cannot be treated in the field,<br /> - cannot be treated quickly enough to matter in the hospital, &amp; therefore<br /> - a character with a full health bar of lethal wounds is as good as dead already (unless there's someone around with supernatural abilities to save them).<br /> <br /> Really, I think the Armory Reloaded hack is the only way to salvage this rule until an erratum for it is written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","user":"Snapdragyn","date":". 01-08-2017, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T20:45:02-08:00","id":1028854,"title":"","content":"There are two ways you can read, &quot;Achieving sufficient successes restores one Health point lost to bashing damage.&quot; It could mean that one health point, which was lost to bashing damage, is restored. Or, it could mean that one health point, which was lost, is restored to bashing damage. Granted, if the intent is the latter, it's a strange way to phrase it, considering it's atypical to describe health points filled with damage as being &quot;lost&quot;, and to describe downgrading lethal damage to bashing as &quot;restoring &quot; but it does explain how stabilizing someone who is bleeding out would be possible, and it keeps the mechanics for emergency care consistent with the later quote, &quot;Note that this treatment does not eliminate wounds. It simply minimizes them.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-08-2017, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T21:13:45-08:00","id":1028860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion?p=1028854#post1028854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are two ways you can read, &quot;Achieving sufficient successes restores one Health point lost to bashing damage.&quot; It could mean that one health point, which was lost to bashing damage, is restored. Or, it could mean that one health point, which was lost, is restored to bashing damage. Granted, if the intent is the latter, it's a strange way to phrase it, considering it's atypical to describe health points filled with damage as being &quot;lost&quot;, and to describe downgrading lethal damage to bashing as &quot;restoring &quot; but it does explain how stabilizing someone who is bleeding out would be possible, and it keeps the mechanics for emergency care consistent with the later quote, &quot;Note that this treatment does not eliminate wounds. It simply minimizes them.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, I can see how that reading would work. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I don't, however, think that resolves the issues of a) having to be in a medical facility to treat a lethal wound at all, nor b) facing one hour per roll when the patient would bleed out &amp; die within minutes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T02:14:26-08:00","id":1028933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snapdragyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion#post1028624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not understand how many successes are needed with the Medicine skill to stabilize someone who is bleeding out. Probably because the rules (or at least the stated rule &amp; proffered example) contradict themselves:<br /> <br /> World of Darkness Storytelling System Rulebook, p.62, 2nd column, 1st complete paragraph in that column, 3rd sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;... a patient who's bleeding to death or in a coma is stabilized if one success is achieved on the roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Same page, same column, 5th paragraph (which starts an Example section), 5th sentence:<br /> <br /> &quot;He must accumulate seven successes to stop the flow of blood and save Emir's life.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, um - WTH? Do you stabilize someone with 1 success, or do you have to get successes = their total health dots? This would make a HUGE difference in a life-or-death situation (seriously, poor Emir almost bleed out &amp; died waiting for those 7 successes).<br /> <br /> Is there an erratum for this somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the first case, a &quot;success&quot; means a &quot;successful feat of stabilizing&quot; which is achieved by scoring as many successes on the number of health points the patient has. Or, a successful extended action, with each roll taking a minute, and with that minute meaning the victim bleeds a little bit more approaching death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T02:49:48-08:00","id":1028937,"title":"","content":"I noticed the same issues you did with 2E stabilization rules - reading strictly RAW, it's literally impossible to save someone from dying when they hit full lethal, since that can only be healed in a hospital, where the interval is an hour, so they'd suffer 60 health points upgrading to agg damage.<br /> <br /> I treat field stabilization as an extended action, requiring successes equal to filled health boxes. Success heals nothing, but stops lethal from ticking over into aggravated. Actual healing requires long-term hospital care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T04:28:38-08:00","id":1028962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion?p=1028937#post1028937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed the same issues you did with 2E stabilization rules - reading strictly RAW, it's literally impossible to save someone from dying when they hit full lethal, since that can only be healed in a hospital, where the interval is an hour, so they'd suffer 60 health points upgrading to agg damage.<br /> <br /> I treat field stabilization as an extended action, requiring successes equal to filled health boxes. Success heals nothing, egbut stops lethal from ticking over into aggravated. Actual healing requires long-term hospital care.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a rather elegant solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:42:09-08:00","id":1029017,"title":"","content":"Since there were no major changes to the Healing rules from nWoD to CofD, (that I could locate - the GMC doesn't have any changes), I think referring to those rules for a clearer picture is a valid option.<br /> <br /> Both books say a Dexteritty + Medicine check can be attempted in the field, or the ER. Both say that achieving &quot;sufficient successes&quot; that equal to the total Health lost &quot;restores one Health point to bashing damage.&quot; My earlier post, and Charlquin's &quot;second interpretation,&quot; suggested that this statement meant that one point downgraded from lethal to bashing. I have since changed my mind, because of that wording. So, Snapdragyn, I think your interpretation of my post is correct.<br /> <br /> However, I think the nWod book does a much better job expounding upon skills. I feel that it's a major part of the CofD book that's lacking - the nWod core book does an excellent job breaking down specific tasks relating to each skill. Maybe the developers left that out of CofD because they figured most players were coming from nWoD and had that as a resource and didn't need to reprint it, or perhaps they were pressed for space with the God Machine Campaign they wanted to add. Who knows.<br /> <br /> But, there's a major piece that is missing from the CofD book, dealing with this very subject. Under the Medicine skill, page 61 of the nWoD core book, it addresses this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Achieving sufficient successes (equal to the total, overall Health points lost by the patient) restores one Health point lost to bashing damage, in addition to any healing that the character already does under his own power. A patient may regain no more that one 'extra' Health point by this means per day. <b>Alternatively, a patient who's bleeding to death or in a coma is stablized if one success is achieved on the roll (The loss of Health points to aggrivated damage each minute is stopped; see 'Incapatation,' p. 173)</b>&quot; (nWod core book, p. 61)<br /> <br /> Since this check can be made in the field, I feel it covers the issue.<br /> <br /> I feel this handles it quite nicely. My previous example of Jack and the nurse is still pretty much valid; the only difference is that Jack would remain at 5 aggrivated and 3 lethal and would not lose any more lethal to aggrivated. The nurse can then call 911 and get an ambulance to Jack where he'll receive proper medical attention in the hospital.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:09:29-08:00","id":1029033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion?p=1028937#post1028937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed the same issues you did with 2E stabilization rules - reading strictly RAW, it's literally impossible to save someone from dying when they hit full lethal, since that can only be healed in a hospital, where the interval is an hour, so they'd suffer 60 health points upgrading to agg damage.<br /> <br /> I treat field stabilization as an extended action, requiring successes equal to filled health boxes. Success heals nothing, but stops lethal from ticking over into aggravated. Actual healing requires long-term hospital care.</div> </div> </div> </div>In real life, if you try to operate on someone without stabilizing them first, they will indubitably die. Stabilization and grand-scale medical treatment are two different things, and systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:17:50-08:00","id":1029042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion?p=1029033#post1029033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In real life, if you try to operate on someone without stabilizing them first, they will indubitably die. Stabilization and grand-scale medical treatment are two different things, and systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why my solution treats them as two different things. There are no actual rules to field stabilize someone in 2E that I could find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:34:22-08:00","id":1029050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Dynel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion?p=1029017#post1029017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since there were no major changes to the Healing rules from nWoD to CofD, (that I could locate - the GMC doesn't have any changes), I think referring to those rules for a clearer picture is a valid option.<br /> <br /> Both books say a Dexteritty + Medicine check can be attempted in the field, or the ER. Both say that achieving &quot;sufficient successes&quot; that equal to the total Health lost &quot;restores one Health point to bashing damage.&quot; My earlier post, and Charlquin's &quot;second interpretation,&quot; suggested that this statement meant that one point downgraded from lethal to bashing. I have since changed my mind, because of that wording. So, Snapdragyn, I think your interpretation of my post is correct.<br /> <br /> However, I think the nWod book does a much better job expounding upon skills. I feel that it's a major part of the CofD book that's lacking - the nWod core book does an excellent job breaking down specific tasks relating to each skill. Maybe the developers left that out of CofD because they figured most players were coming from nWoD and had that as a resource and didn't need to reprint it, or perhaps they were pressed for space with the God Machine Campaign they wanted to add. Who knows.<br /> <br /> But, there's a major piece that is missing from the CofD book, dealing with this very subject. Under the Medicine skill, page 61 of the nWoD core book, it addresses this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Achieving sufficient successes (equal to the total, overall Health points lost by the patient) restores one Health point lost to bashing damage, in addition to any healing that the character already does under his own power. A patient may regain no more that one 'extra' Health point by this means per day. <b>Alternatively, a patient who's bleeding to death or in a coma is stablized if one success is achieved on the roll (The loss of Health points to aggrivated damage each minute is stopped; see 'Incapatation,' p. 173)</b>&quot; (nWod core book, p. 61)<br /> <br /> Since this check can be made in the field, I feel it covers the issue.<br /> <br /> I feel this handles it quite nicely. My previous example of Jack and the nurse is still pretty much valid; the only difference is that Jack would remain at 5 aggrivated and 3 lethal and would not lose any more lethal to aggrivated. The nurse can then call 911 and get an ambulance to Jack where he'll receive proper medical attention in the hospital.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much agree that the CofD rules are lacking on skills descriptions.<br /> <br /> This gets back to my original post, however - the nWoD stated '1 success' rule on p.61 is immediately contradicted in the text. I've since found that this not only happens in the example (where, yeah, rules override examples in cases of conflict), BUT also in the detailed rules breakdown of roll results on p.62.<br /> <br /> An example: &quot;Until you acquire the total number of successes required to stop a patient from bleeding to death, one more of his wounds turns from lethal to aggravated per minute.&quot; (And additional similar quotes within the same section.)<br /> <br /> This says 'total number of successES', plural. So now we have 2 places (once in an example, then multiple times within the roll results section) that reference multiple successes on an extended action, vs. a single sentence declaring 1 success needed.<br /> <br /> I think the nWoD error here was the 1 success statement, &amp; it didn't get caught in editing. The CofD error is that no rule even exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12661-snapdragyn","name":"Snapdragyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T10:16:04-08:00","id":1029137,"title":"","content":"I <i>think </i>this is the key phrase:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When a character\u2019s rightmost Health box has lethal damage marked in it, he takes another point of damage each minute (upgrading existing lethal damage to aggravated) <i><b>until he receives medical attention, mundane or supernatural.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much up for interpretation, but: I think the idea is, <i>any </i>medical attention will stabilize you; or, to put it another way, narratively speaking, if you get some medical attention, the game system assumes you're not going to bleed out, unless the doctor/medic screws up. Be that a successful first aid roll, or getting you into surgery<br /> <br /> Or, to put it yet another way, while I agree that it's probably an oversight that it's not more specific, that makes sense to me. The game doesn't want you to die for weird mechanical loopholes.<br /> <br /> However, that &quot;restored to bashing damage&quot; is definitely weird. I think Charlaquin is right, or else (under a very literal interpretation of the rules) first aid is literally impossible if you're full up on lethal. From Lord Dynel's post, it looks like it was a phrase replicated from first edition that wasn't clarified.<br /> <br /> Edit: To put it yet another another way, a weird subsystem error got cut in favour of a narrative thing (assuming it was intentional).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 01-09-2017, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T11:54:23-08:00","id":1029186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snapdragyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion?p=1029050#post1029050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very much agree that the CofD rules are lacking on skills descriptions.<br /> <br /> This gets back to my original post, however - the nWoD stated '1 success' rule on p.61 is immediately contradicted in the text. I've since found that this not only happens in the example (where, yeah, rules override examples in cases of conflict), BUT also in the detailed rules breakdown of roll results on p.62.<br /> <br /> An example: &quot;Until you acquire the total number of successes required to stop a patient from bleeding to death, one more of his wounds turns from lethal to aggravated per minute.&quot; (And additional similar quotes within the same section.)<br /> <br /> This says 'total number of successES', plural. So now we have 2 places (once in an example, then multiple times within the roll results section) that reference multiple successes on an extended action, vs. a single sentence declaring 1 success needed.<br /> <br /> I think the nWoD error here was the 1 success statement, &amp; it didn't get caught in editing. The CofD error is that no rule even exists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with you, that there is some error with the &quot;one success&quot; statement. Honestly, I think the example is correct - it's awfully detailed to be erroneous, in my opinion. Interestingly, the &quot;one success&quot; wording is gone from the CofD book.<br /> <br /> So, I think the rules are there in the CofD book, I just think you have to infer more than you do in the nWoD (because of the extended explanation and the example). If you read the healing entry on page 61 of the nWoD book, then read the healing section on page 95 of the<br /> <br /> Page 95 of the CofD book tells us:<ul><li>If you're Health pool's rightmost box has bashing, you need to roll Stamina every round of fall unconscious, which will heal in 15 minutes.</li> <li>If all the Health boxes are full of lethal, that doesn't heal by itself, and you're bleeding out. You need prompt medical attention. Otherwise you upgrade one point of lethal to aggravated every minute until attended to or dead.</li> </ul><br /> Page 96 of the CofD books tells us:<ul><li>Medical care is an extended action, and you need a number of successes equal to the damage suffered by the patient.</li> <li>Medical care can be done in the field or ER (Dexterity + Medicine) with an interval of 1 minute, or in hospital care (Intelligence + Medicine), with an interval of 1 hour.</li> <li>Achieving &quot;sufficient success&quot; (which infer successes = to current damage total) on one of these checks can recover a point of bashing damage, plus damage that normally heals over time.</li> <li>Hospital care can downgrade wounds by one degree, focusing on the worst damage first. Only one wound per day can be downgraded this way.</li> </ul><br /> Page 61 of the nWoD book tells us:<ul><li>Dexterity + Medicine is rolled when a patient is dying, when trying to stabilize the patient.</li> <li>According to the example - which demonstrates a character who has taken full lethal damage - after an amount of Dexterity + Medicine successes equal to the damage total are made, the patient/victim is stabilized. He does not gain any Health back, but stops upgrading lethal to aggravated. We can infer from this the rule as it is intended.</li> </ul><br /> I think the &quot;one success&quot; statement can be dropped. I think these points cover everything, does it not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12124,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","user":"Lord Dynel","date":". 01-09-2017, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12124-lord-dynel","name":"Lord Dynel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T14:03:23-08:00","id":1029249,"title":"","content":"The thing I don't particularly like about the extended roll having a target equal to health boxes is that hardier characters are tougher to save. Theoretically they have more rolls before they bleed out, but since extended actions only get rolls equal to the attribute + skill pool your average first responder is only going to roll three or four times before they're out of chances, regardless of whether the victim has six health boxes or ten. To that end I've been running it as a flat target of 5 successes on an extended roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T14:47:19-08:00","id":1029271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028624-medicine-skill-confusion?p=1029249#post1029249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I don't particularly like about the extended roll having a target equal to health boxes is that hardier characters are tougher to save. Theoretically they have more rolls before they bleed out, but since extended actions only get rolls equal to the attribute + skill pool your average first responder is only going to roll three or four times before they're out of chances, regardless of whether the victim has six health boxes or ten. To that end I've been running it as a flat target of 5 successes on an extended roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it also takes more serious injuries to get hardier characters to the point where they need such medical attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T15:10:59-08:00","id":1029284,"title":"","content":"This isn't based off of a reading of the rules, confusing or not, but if you want the character to have a chance at survival without somehow downgrading damage in the field you could apply something like the advanced duration rules to your heal check. In this case every success on the first aid check would extend the amount of time it takes for each lethal point to change to aggravated, thus buying time for the character to undergo surgery in a hospital. One minute becomes ten with one success, perhaps twenty with two or an hour with three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}